    {
      "title": "'Witch-hunt is underway': Sonam Wangchuk on notice to HIAL school",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/witch-hunt-is-underway-sonam-wangchuk-on-notice-to-hial-school-126110500007_1.html",
      "description": "Educationist Sonam Wangchuk on Wednesday slammed the Ladakh administration, accusing it of pursuing a policy of \"witch-hunt\" against institutions and individuals questioning its decisions and alleging that the action against HIAL and its school was part of an attempt to \"silence dissent\" in the region.\nReacting to the notice directing Himalayan Institute of Alternatives, Ladakh (HIAL) to halt activities related to Desert Flower School at Phyang, Wangchuk questioned the administration's priorities, drawing a sharp contrast between the restrictions allegedly imposed on educational institutions and the relaxation of rules governing liquor establishments in the Union Territory.\n\"Stop education, prevent children from becoming educated, keep schools closed, but make alcohol more accessible and push the entire region towards alcoholism. This is how these policies appear to us,\" Wangchuk, accompanied by his wife Gitanjali J Angmo, co-founder and CEO of HIAL, told reporters in Leh.\nQuestioni",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-05T02:25:08"
    }
